      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t the value for bEndpointAddress come from the interface descriptor? I would suggest looking for the first IN and the first OUT endpoint that can be found in the interface descriptor, similar to how it\u0027s done at https://github.com/pyusb/pyusb/blob/master/docs/tutorial.rst#lets-get-it-started\nAs the code stands, it assumes that for a given interface, the two values for bEndpointAddress are 0x81 + bInterfaceNumber and 0x1 + bInterfaceNumber. This assumption might be true for a specific device, but I\u0027m not sure if there\u0027s a guarantee for this.",
